.TH from "" "Command"
.SH NAME
from \- generate a list of numbers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfrom \fIstart \fBto \fIstop \fB[by \fIincr\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
from -- generate list of numbers
Usage:	from start to stop [ by incr ]
'start', 'stop' and 'incr' (default: 1) are decimal integers with optional '-'.
.HE
.B from
prints, one per line, the sequence of integers starting at
.I start
and continuing by steps of
.I incr
(default: 1) up to and including
.IR stop ,
in either direction.
The literal words
.B to
and
.B by
must appear exactly as shown.
.PP
Each of
.IR start ,
.IR stop ,
and
.I incr
is a decimal integer, optionally preceded by
.BR \- .
.I incr
must have the same sign as
.IR stop \- start
(or be omitted, giving the default of 1); a zero
.I incr
is also rejected.
.PP
.B from
is typically used inside a shell loop, for example
.DS
for i in `from 0 to 7`
do
	/etc/mknod /dev/hs0$i c 7 $i
done
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B sh
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B from
prints a usage message and exits with status 1 if the arguments do
not have one of the two accepted forms, if
.B to
or
.B by
is missing or misspelled, if a numeric argument is not a valid
signed integer, or if
.I incr
is zero or has the wrong sign for the requested direction.
